cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the paper it accompanies (below). If you need to refer to a
  specific version of the code itself, cite the archived release and its DOI.
title: >-
  Analysis code for "Delivery and Attitude Modulate Shared Neural Processing of Speech Through
  Distinct Frequency Channels"
abstract: >-
  Frequency-resolved inter-subject correlation of magnetoencephalography during naturalistic
  speech: source reconstruction, leave-one-out ISC by frequency band, low-level acoustic and
  visual feature control, separation of periodic from aperiodic activity, region-of-interest
  enrichment and against-zero tests, and the figures reported in the paper.
type: software
